> On Friday, July 26, 2013 12:01:20 AM UTC-7, Janis wrote:
>> Instead of writing more than one Elbereth in one attempt (which can require
>> more than one turn), write Elbereth, then add Elbereth to existing writing,
>> and add more as desired. 
> That's what I did, and it proved fatal:
>   Do you want to add to the current engraving? [ynq] (y) 
>   You add to the writing in the dust with your fingers.
>   What do you want to add to the writing in the dust here? 
>   Something is written here in the dust.
>   You read: "E|bercthE|bfreth".
>   You see no objects here.
>   What do you want to write with? [- abny or ?*] 
>   Do you want to add to the current engraving? [ynq] (y) 
>   You add to the writing in the dust with your fingers.
>   What do you want to add to the writing in the dust here? 
>   Something is written here in the dust.
>   You read: "E|bercthE|bfrethElberctQ".
>   You see no objects here.
Sounds like that would have been the point to reconsider (i.e. run),
especially since you knew that the dwarf would get an action now.  At
the very beginning, statistics was well in your favour (0.27^4, i.e 0.5%
of failure).  But at this point, knowing the history, the chance of
failure was already up to 0.27^1, i.e. 27%.  (Not that I'd always
consider this kind of advice in my own games…)

>   What do you want to write with? [- abny or ?*] 
>   Do you want to add to the current engraving? [ynq] (y) 
>   You add to the writing in the dust with your fingers.
>   What do you want to add to the writing in the dust here? 
>   The dwarf thrusts his dwarvish short sword.
>   The dwarf hits!
>   You die...
> 
> I think it was quite unlikely that I was going to fail on 4 consecutive tries to write Elbereth, but quite unlikely stuff happens in nethack.
> Since a dwarf only fights every other turn, I think in the first turn after the dwarf swings, I should attempt an "ElberethElbereth", and if that doesn't work, I should then try adding "Elbereth".  I think that would allow me to write an extra Elbereth for every dwarf swing.  Right? 

